Hey Muse for Portal includes code derived from other open-source projects. The app as a whole is
MIT (LICENSE); the parts below keep their own licenses.

TECHO5 and EchoLocal
  This repository is a fork of hey-muse (https://github.com/wobsoriano/hey-muse), itself a fork of
  TECHO5 (https://github.com/HuskerMinion/techo5) by HuskerMinion, which is built on EchoLocal by Yuri
  Gelfand. Both MIT. The Go core keeps code from them: the end-of-utterance detector
  (core/endpoint), the cloud voice client (core/speech), the timer, alarm and volume tools
  (core/device, from echod/internal/feature/assistant and config), the connection and pairing
  lifecycle (core/heymuse, from echod/internal/feature/muse) and the voice turn (core/heymuse/turn.go,
  from echod/internal/feature/voice/muse.go). Everything of TECHO5's that runs an Echo — the Linux
  image, the daemon, the setup page — is left out.

Muse client and Bluetooth setup (core/muse, core/muse/pairing)
  Muse Gadget SDK, Apache License 2.0
  Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
  https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk, at commit
  b9008abba7dc4109c66212b9b82e459d08b98b85. These files are hey-muse's ports to Go of the SDK's Linux
  client (linux/src/musegadget), each changed from its source, and each says at its top which SDK file
  it came from and what was changed:
    - core/muse: api.go, client.go, envelope.go, muse.go, proto.go, session.go and turn.go, from
      muse_api.py, service.py, executor.py, identity.py, config.py, link_client.py and noise/
      (envelope.py, framing.py, transport.py, _proto.py). session.go and turn.go add the chat
      subscription, reply matching and voice notes, which the Linux client does not have and the
      SDK's ESP32 firmware does (esp32/components/muse).
    - core/muse/pairing: framing.go, gatt.go, messages.go, network.go, session.go, setup.go and
      verify.go, from ble_framing.py, ble_server.py, identity.py, pairing.py, ble_setup.py,
      network.py, cli.py and muse_api.py.
    - app/.../BlePeripheral.kt serves the GATT shape of ble_server.py on Android.
  Test vectors, core/muse/pairing/testdata/link_pairing_v5.json (not shipped in the app): copied
  unchanged from linux/tests/vectors/link_pairing_v5.json.
  The license in full is core/muse/LICENSE. The SDK ships no NOTICE file.
  Not covered, and not here: Meta says the SDK's Apache license does not cover its default avatar,
  so neither the character nor the code that draws it is in this repository or in the app.
  tools/muse-avatar/make_sprites.py builds the pictures from the user's own SDK checkout.
  This app is not made or endorsed by Meta. Muse and Portal are Meta's.

Built-in voice (app/src/main/cpp/pico, app/src/main/assets/pico)
  SVOX Pico — Apache License 2.0
  Copyright (C) 2008-2009 SVOX AG, Baslerstr. 30, 8048 Zuerich, Switzerland.
  The speech engine and its U.S. English voice data, en-US_ta.bin and en-US_lh0_sg.bin, taken from
  https://github.com/naggety/picotts. Changes: picopltf.h takes the byte order from the compiler
